  <h2>1. Authorized use</h2>
  <p>OrgVitals is a read-only Salesforce org health scanner published by <strong>CloudAlgo Private Limited</strong>. You may only connect and scan a Salesforce org that you own, administer, or have <strong>explicit written authorization</strong> to assess. It is your responsibility to confirm you have the necessary permission before you connect any org.</p>

  <h2>2. Prohibited use</h2>
  <p>You must not use OrgVitals to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>probe, scan, monitor, or attack Salesforce orgs that you do not own, administer, or have explicit written authorization to assess;</li>
    <li>attempt to access, copy, or infer data that you are not authorised to access;</li>
    <li>circumvent, bypass, or defeat Salesforce security, access controls, or the read-only nature of the tool;</li>
    <li>use the app for any unlawful purpose or in violation of Salesforce's or Anthropic's terms;</li>
    <li>share, sell, or transfer your account or credentials, or allow unauthorised persons to use them; or</li>
    <li>reverse engineer the app to build or assist in building a competing product, except to the extent such restriction is prohibited by applicable law.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Your credentials</h2>
  <p>You are responsible for keeping your Salesforce CLI authentication, your Anthropic API key, and your account credentials secure, and for all activity conducted through them.</p>

  <h2>4. Consequences</h2>
  <p>Violating this policy may result in the suspension or termination of your access to OrgVitals, with or without notice, and may expose you to legal liability. This policy supplements, and is incorporated into, the <a href="/products/orgvitals/legal/terms">Terms of Service</a>.</p>

  <h2>5. Reporting &amp; contact</h2>
  <p>To report misuse, or if you have questions about acceptable use, contact <a href="mailto:contact@cloudalgo.com">contact@cloudalgo.com</a>.</p>

